[{:db/id "q-93672/selection/99b77e619f3ff328474f1ff1331b4895911bc36054c083665839ca05a1a9e570" :answer/id #uuid "19937a44-a0ff-511a-be4a-3514548e5bf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+Bx{e}^{-3x}+\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93672/selection/f52aacd23c8efd21bd5847c497c29776506e5aa33bc87be2dba96479597df6ea" :answer/id #uuid "4bbf711b-4858-5f16-b5cf-f68396e1a314" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+Bx{e}^{-3x}+\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93672/selection/effb7fcc7f454715a7e8df3e4ac73721f48cbe9e971bfa63b6282adb46fdd363" :answer/id #uuid "dbea8af9-499a-5e6b-baa4-f26e3331585b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{3x}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93672/selection/7df5d68907d1f3f2693768961624f946c07ae1063d205efe030f19cfc837574d" :answer/id #uuid "69619610-e793-5c12-91fd-83a133f5188e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+Bx{e}^{-3x}+6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93672/selection/cb558e10ffc9f46e94bcf14e6e11b6221e4814d811aff0f452cc3dd2359a9326" :answer/id #uuid "8b5b057c-bbb7-5248-97ac-136a7cc077b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{3x}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93672/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "304b2665-d148-54cd-bf73-9d35f5996a59" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93672/selection/f52aacd23c8efd21bd5847c497c29776506e5aa33bc87be2dba96479597df6ea" :answer-field/choices ["q-93672/selection/99b77e619f3ff328474f1ff1331b4895911bc36054c083665839ca05a1a9e570" "q-93672/selection/f52aacd23c8efd21bd5847c497c29776506e5aa33bc87be2dba96479597df6ea" "q-93672/selection/effb7fcc7f454715a7e8df3e4ac73721f48cbe9e971bfa63b6282adb46fdd363" "q-93672/selection/7df5d68907d1f3f2693768961624f946c07ae1063d205efe030f19cfc837574d" "q-93672/selection/cb558e10ffc9f46e94bcf14e6e11b6221e4814d811aff0f452cc3dd2359a9326"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93672" :question/id #uuid "f7a0a468-1c88-521a-84b2-9f5ade22295f" :question/math-academy-id "q-93672" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+6\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+9y=3.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+6\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+9y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+6\\lambda +9 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-3$ is a repeated root, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-3x}+Bx{e}^{-3x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $0.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $0,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=0,\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=0\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\alpha ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+0+9\\alpha =3\\,⟹\\,\\alpha =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}+Bx{e}^{-3x}+\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-93672/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3438d77-c314-5b0a-b1f1-9ae4a3f970b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93672"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93669/selection/5ce3795bafcce1b5a496fcd927bf1db7b677af9725735082a6e78f8e84e04d3a" :answer/id #uuid "0c70f383-0715-5c8b-a3f3-9df7ff8f736f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{4x}+Bx{e}^{4x}+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93669/selection/0ebe84e6bc58bb0b8b9af79480be341f26fb17647f06b5d6c70b3e427e4579fe" :answer/id #uuid "734ec4ef-42ae-5de9-9117-5cf6638ef440" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{2x}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93669/selection/87b49b71a0f25166977078c982b1d604b8c88665012d63584c7c4aa7a5409930" :answer/id #uuid "09e21cb6-826c-5baf-a418-c1a2e0363f67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-4x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93669/selection/f083b23dc6190ea71297cf4e01d839448c04ccf72fd4988b9dade0dc249b364c" :answer/id #uuid "655de9ea-d8fd-5ec3-9bdf-3ea2154fbed8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{2x}-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93669/selection/b0b5b4535937803420ffbecf0674616c48f2252163013e4f287164227fd1a7c0" :answer/id #uuid "5d25de67-1e4a-59f1-8484-f49fe39593c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{2x}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93669/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "56fb338c-93a1-58b8-8ae9-a76c71bac543" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93669/selection/f083b23dc6190ea71297cf4e01d839448c04ccf72fd4988b9dade0dc249b364c" :answer-field/choices ["q-93669/selection/5ce3795bafcce1b5a496fcd927bf1db7b677af9725735082a6e78f8e84e04d3a" "q-93669/selection/0ebe84e6bc58bb0b8b9af79480be341f26fb17647f06b5d6c70b3e427e4579fe" "q-93669/selection/87b49b71a0f25166977078c982b1d604b8c88665012d63584c7c4aa7a5409930" "q-93669/selection/f083b23dc6190ea71297cf4e01d839448c04ccf72fd4988b9dade0dc249b364c" "q-93669/selection/b0b5b4535937803420ffbecf0674616c48f2252163013e4f287164227fd1a7c0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93669" :question/id #uuid "7e3900ba-b694-5263-b920-c3f6f1480f74" :question/math-academy-id "q-93669" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8y=4.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -8 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-4$ or $\\lambda =2$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $0.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $0,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=0,\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=0\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\alpha ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+0-8\\alpha =4\\,⟹\\,\\alpha =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{2x}-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-93669/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3438d77-c314-5b0a-b1f1-9ae4a3f970b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93669"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7904/selection/da68b243ca9ea9583655249a53af923c993fd0f9f525b3ab1b9147d2d74f36de" :answer/id #uuid "15cf578a-442e-545a-9dd8-c81e00f86e0a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7904/selection/40f43bdfb5b567c6b3608bdc2de70a4c6abbb7c637e35797d9663e964cb12b74" :answer/id #uuid "3d83ef38-e818-5e95-a2c8-0b75bbf23941" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7904/selection/e713fa36c48be56dee9223f02b12ea84e75552724250a4e130a6b01ea8c2dd61" :answer/id #uuid "bfd71c86-d57b-5c64-8e81-16e29f15cc6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7904/selection/85bae096b1f8874be0b76620674c62ea31fab97efec020eb9b81667c7bd81bae" :answer/id #uuid "105ff811-c432-5482-9056-8bbfa0646e30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7904/selection/d626406c1fa5f32381fee42897865248e432c493326c0ce8143b2b90b0584800" :answer/id #uuid "1be3491e-6126-5b7e-9b24-6b2dd791eb35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7904/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "054f6bc4-e22f-5eab-a5fe-05eaf8e96d74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-7904/selection/e713fa36c48be56dee9223f02b12ea84e75552724250a4e130a6b01ea8c2dd61" :answer-field/choices ["q-7904/selection/da68b243ca9ea9583655249a53af923c993fd0f9f525b3ab1b9147d2d74f36de" "q-7904/selection/40f43bdfb5b567c6b3608bdc2de70a4c6abbb7c637e35797d9663e964cb12b74" "q-7904/selection/e713fa36c48be56dee9223f02b12ea84e75552724250a4e130a6b01ea8c2dd61" "q-7904/selection/85bae096b1f8874be0b76620674c62ea31fab97efec020eb9b81667c7bd81bae" "q-7904/selection/d626406c1fa5f32381fee42897865248e432c493326c0ce8143b2b90b0584800"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7904" :question/id #uuid "b95c671b-321a-50e6-94b2-76f7485353a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-7904" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+16y=-4.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+16y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-16 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $0.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $0,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=0,\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=0\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\alpha ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+16\\alpha =-4\\,⟹\\,\\alpha =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-7904/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3438d77-c314-5b0a-b1f1-9ae4a3f970b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7904"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7896/selection/1c6478bb834d9b203cd569bc2b9366de7cb94867f99b04945ee7981570bc8d38" :answer/id #uuid "a06f759d-32e0-56f8-8dd0-8f0dad8184d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{2x}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7896/selection/c91d3c4785bd83f71d356a020d45135fe72dc949a17a740785363c7dff9f6ade" :answer/id #uuid "3c4bbd75-ea77-5dcb-8f35-634361045560" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{2x}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7896/selection/19aca14a37f532861604457396761351b6f568eb73faa9b25f3023a1b186b337" :answer/id #uuid "148c5c16-2241-5c67-9a75-598f367b0107" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{2x}-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7896/selection/92ea6bdac8a595e7c86be6e67c922f71fc88a347a2197f34cb95c0627a8e95b9" :answer/id #uuid "53bdafdd-558a-5c66-a4d0-e29a1a25f254" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{2x}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7896/selection/8c02b77518d4b4dcca4ce687056d6686c48fd1d78a1421fca2e1caf11c62d6e2" :answer/id #uuid "18be48d5-dd34-58dd-93c0-a62de2eda03c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{-2x}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7896/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "79c8147f-4ebd-5c45-8a45-a9c70343d484" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-7896/selection/c91d3c4785bd83f71d356a020d45135fe72dc949a17a740785363c7dff9f6ade" :answer-field/choices ["q-7896/selection/1c6478bb834d9b203cd569bc2b9366de7cb94867f99b04945ee7981570bc8d38" "q-7896/selection/c91d3c4785bd83f71d356a020d45135fe72dc949a17a740785363c7dff9f6ade" "q-7896/selection/19aca14a37f532861604457396761351b6f568eb73faa9b25f3023a1b186b337" "q-7896/selection/92ea6bdac8a595e7c86be6e67c922f71fc88a347a2197f34cb95c0627a8e95b9" "q-7896/selection/8c02b77518d4b4dcca4ce687056d6686c48fd1d78a1421fca2e1caf11c62d6e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7896" :question/id #uuid "c2fba9ca-a181-507b-8602-6d18bc6141a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-7896" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-6y=12.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-6y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -6 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-3$ or $\\lambda =2$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{2x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $0.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $0,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=0,\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=0\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\alpha ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+0-6\\alpha =12\\,⟹\\,\\alpha =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-2.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{2x}-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-7896/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3438d77-c314-5b0a-b1f1-9ae4a3f970b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7896"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93668/selection/0e1b6d977bea7a765edcff76170f6393355eb1c767a6f9db1834cdf12becb7c0" :answer/id #uuid "a0dc5d18-6e76-5584-b7c9-3f75619e489f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}(x)=10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93668/selection/2e17d9a71b6510f5b6854a5ba074e235d17799f91fe55f2c9542522898268ec9" :answer/id #uuid "592eeb51-4247-50d9-9280-ae13bc2e431d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}(x)=3x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93668/selection/e40363db8aff07c522087f18ab9cbf9a493f553e12a59bc410eb2120a13b27a7" :answer/id #uuid "2d3a96bf-2007-5760-9224-3a935ce21038" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}(x)=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93668/selection/62af2258d8f10dbdd2749da38c3877e6d87e6cde2df46e120f89b217c9b28ef6" :answer/id #uuid "91c96f37-819b-52ef-a7ae-c558be6d35d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}(x)=-2x+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93668/selection/30db871cef003dddefb99cb31b61d8641cdfbbccfebba7876db4f8b8d0ecab11" :answer/id #uuid "0c4aedbc-85dd-57e4-9f28-92457f9dcf1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}(x)=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93668/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "53ecebbc-de9e-5e0f-a98d-d286c988b214" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93668/selection/e40363db8aff07c522087f18ab9cbf9a493f553e12a59bc410eb2120a13b27a7" :answer-field/choices ["q-93668/selection/0e1b6d977bea7a765edcff76170f6393355eb1c767a6f9db1834cdf12becb7c0" "q-93668/selection/2e17d9a71b6510f5b6854a5ba074e235d17799f91fe55f2c9542522898268ec9" "q-93668/selection/e40363db8aff07c522087f18ab9cbf9a493f553e12a59bc410eb2120a13b27a7" "q-93668/selection/62af2258d8f10dbdd2749da38c3877e6d87e6cde2df46e120f89b217c9b28ef6" "q-93668/selection/30db871cef003dddefb99cb31b61d8641cdfbbccfebba7876db4f8b8d0ecab11"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93668" :question/id #uuid "f079ad1b-3fa4-5b05-93e6-15c915d68e55" :question/math-academy-id "q-93668" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5y=20\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)={e}^{-x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x),$ find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." :question/worked-solution "The right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $0.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $0,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ is a constant that is to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=0,\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=0\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\alpha ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0+0+5\\alpha =20\\,⟹\\,\\alpha =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93668/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3438d77-c314-5b0a-b1f1-9ae4a3f970b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93668"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-64285/selection/d268783d58fb00ac912fe2ef48483bd0682afb3e107788eec1f6ae87f853d38c" :answer/id #uuid "9346bdbc-9a23-5d8a-b079-02bfb56d9557" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=x-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64285/selection/58ba1cc3501f5340905a7c1f9873c4d29e49ff794d06174d44c86f08d725d94f" :answer/id #uuid "be31ed43-cd2f-5ea8-a547-2547eaaf5b90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=2x-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64285/selection/9a6fecacc26fed9a1704e11e136e3b9bbdb74695a489caec89328c6f7d9b1fce" :answer/id #uuid "2383eb63-78b9-59bb-a6cf-709331f3508d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-x-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64285/selection/560337abed267034f50095628980d49a0f8e37322c7f4dac4e2f4355220e31c9" :answer/id #uuid "32fbf00c-e271-5865-a47f-dc7db54f192f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=\\frac{x}{5}-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64285/selection/ff76ff340394414fd32856c0ef4d81c0ceec5818737dbdf45ec8e0bfaaaeccc6" :answer/id #uuid "608a9e08-fbc2-57aa-af12-f7d43b530bb5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}_{p}=-x+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64285/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "94dfcbb3-2a5c-5e2c-85ef-2079e2a27601" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64285/selection/d268783d58fb00ac912fe2ef48483bd0682afb3e107788eec1f6ae87f853d38c" :answer-field/choices ["q-64285/selection/d268783d58fb00ac912fe2ef48483bd0682afb3e107788eec1f6ae87f853d38c" "q-64285/selection/58ba1cc3501f5340905a7c1f9873c4d29e49ff794d06174d44c86f08d725d94f" "q-64285/selection/9a6fecacc26fed9a1704e11e136e3b9bbdb74695a489caec89328c6f7d9b1fce" "q-64285/selection/560337abed267034f50095628980d49a0f8e37322c7f4dac4e2f4355220e31c9" "q-64285/selection/ff76ff340394414fd32856c0ef4d81c0ceec5818737dbdf45ec8e0bfaaaeccc6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64285" :question/id #uuid "3d511e4f-8803-5021-b5c2-53a7b4de5acf" :question/math-academy-id "q-64285" :question/problem "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y=-5x+6\n$$\n\nhas the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{5x}+B{e}^{-x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation." :question/worked-solution "The right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $1,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha x+\\beta \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha ,\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=0\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$  and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n0-4\\alpha -5(\\alpha x+\\beta )=-5x+6\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives:\n\n$$\n-5\\alpha x+(-4\\alpha -5\\beta )=-5x+6\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-5\\alpha =-5\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ -4\\alpha -5\\beta =6\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =1,\\,\\beta =-2.$\n\nTherefore, the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=x-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-64285/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d86b46c0-e30d-525b-b84e-f8296c78aa8b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64285"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93812/selection/6db50521a58e105e2d09f1d803308b95e04e62b1ff7c659e663578a04f280815" :answer/id #uuid "0cdca85f-8cb5-5a40-b972-72d608d9ea94" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-4x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)-\\frac{x}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93812/selection/256b4b4ff723763f1a2fbe219305e4ee3c46f68c75b5d9490c52f6bc6d945b41" :answer/id #uuid "6bc7096e-d78c-5c37-8faf-54b050328eab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{4x}-x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93812/selection/6d7e1c9c25a0b42c7be0a1510bace623a10698cd098dcdc553cf50ea9bac3525" :answer/id #uuid "8f2cc807-bec3-54a6-99ec-0cdab4c31f5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{4x}-\\frac{x}{2}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93812/selection/6ec477af766ace90c1b081f7dba487d980820ac3bb0acfccbde9b62ebe4f9f85" :answer/id #uuid "f6b35ce3-393a-533a-a362-d3edbb331cf4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y={e}^{-4x}(P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93812/selection/c260adc1fc3567fc34c98dd5ada85e2cd875226bc486d40aaed2bd414f0dfd50" :answer/id #uuid "b5a7e6a6-03f3-52ed-becd-e4e5231f4059" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{4x}-2x+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93812/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d78200f-a454-56ad-b022-d0acba8b963c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93812/selection/6d7e1c9c25a0b42c7be0a1510bace623a10698cd098dcdc553cf50ea9bac3525" :answer-field/choices ["q-93812/selection/6db50521a58e105e2d09f1d803308b95e04e62b1ff7c659e663578a04f280815" "q-93812/selection/256b4b4ff723763f1a2fbe219305e4ee3c46f68c75b5d9490c52f6bc6d945b41" "q-93812/selection/6d7e1c9c25a0b42c7be0a1510bace623a10698cd098dcdc553cf50ea9bac3525" "q-93812/selection/6ec477af766ace90c1b081f7dba487d980820ac3bb0acfccbde9b62ebe4f9f85" "q-93812/selection/c260adc1fc3567fc34c98dd5ada85e2cd875226bc486d40aaed2bd414f0dfd50"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93812" :question/id #uuid "d2c91d5d-1887-52e2-b19f-c23ea4f54318" :question/math-academy-id "q-93812" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-16y=8x-32.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-16y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-4$ or $\\lambda =4$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{4x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $1,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha x+\\beta \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha ,\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=0\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n0-16(\\alpha x+\\beta )=8x-32\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-16\\alpha x-16\\beta =8x-32.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-16\\alpha =8\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ -16\\beta =-32\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{1}{2},\\beta =2.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{x}{2}+2.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{4x}-\\frac{x}{2}+2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-93812/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d86b46c0-e30d-525b-b84e-f8296c78aa8b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93812"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-93811/selection/66202b68e1427a74837efbb74ba26ef74b151866c8fc908721b9fb53e258e5f8" :answer/id #uuid "09adaf32-b70d-5020-a894-c96bef42b425" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{3x}-x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93811/selection/c3c47542300b714ace1d8473561255b398dde8d4823fb9def2154337ad442a0f" :answer/id #uuid "3fd39c46-3b81-5294-800c-eba62f77e67b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{3x}-x+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93811/selection/5e9d2783de69bca01535031c059fbc8174c6a6083326c25ff9a813ec51da6e0a" :answer/id #uuid "e0348ac0-bb22-51ad-9366-dfec16525369" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{3x}-x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93811/selection/7a5dd817aefc8c72aaf93c5d2ce7e55f36ceca6821b01df107f4e3d21c9046d2" :answer/id #uuid "507b9e22-3723-59b7-bb99-0dfa492551b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{3x}-3x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93811/selection/9dbec15d4c2a3866624188a9ea566dd3b1200552b13f55a7e3e0826ae53c7107" :answer/id #uuid "17eaa144-855c-579f-958e-69ada1212473" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{3x}-3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93811/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6fc01c58-48df-54e4-bbfc-30e7e3ee11ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93811/selection/9dbec15d4c2a3866624188a9ea566dd3b1200552b13f55a7e3e0826ae53c7107" :answer-field/choices ["q-93811/selection/66202b68e1427a74837efbb74ba26ef74b151866c8fc908721b9fb53e258e5f8" "q-93811/selection/c3c47542300b714ace1d8473561255b398dde8d4823fb9def2154337ad442a0f" "q-93811/selection/5e9d2783de69bca01535031c059fbc8174c6a6083326c25ff9a813ec51da6e0a" "q-93811/selection/7a5dd817aefc8c72aaf93c5d2ce7e55f36ceca6821b01df107f4e3d21c9046d2" "q-93811/selection/9dbec15d4c2a3866624188a9ea566dd3b1200552b13f55a7e3e0826ae53c7107"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93811" :question/id #uuid "9d71200d-b565-5b6c-93a9-0d26e985c2e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-93811" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-6y=18x+3.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-6y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-2$ or $\\lambda =3,$ and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $1,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha x+\\beta \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha ,\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=0\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n0-\\alpha -6(\\alpha x+\\beta )=18x+3\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-6\\alpha x+(-\\alpha -6\\beta )=18x+3.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-6\\alpha =18\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ -\\alpha -6\\beta =3\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-3,\\beta =0.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-3x.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{3x}-3x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-93811/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d86b46c0-e30d-525b-b84e-f8296c78aa8b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93811"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7897/selection/355cbdfc9a6b0fbfcec874529de1ee8dfc88ace13e9d7d4cc3bacfcf53c8e7c3" :answer/id #uuid "d7164818-4a5d-5bd5-934b-d970dc128da8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{x}-2x+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7897/selection/e9af41dd1d69a404c130f636a36b576e034bd76278dbe883bc938617e95e59b7" :answer/id #uuid "f2883814-5631-50c1-b466-f7456529b7d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{-x}-x-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7897/selection/ffdccedf006adb8d8c243369eaddc427f13a1ea0b11bf6c832a0ffb93d6dcf95" :answer/id #uuid "1c28ddac-c82d-56d7-b283-a4e4c25e6372" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{2x}+B{e}^{-x}-x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7897/selection/66c5631fedcddabdceaad5086f58076ab48c53bc77d675665bfc4d76a9439ce6" :answer/id #uuid "245f28f3-1ddd-502d-8462-377f891489a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{x}-x-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7897/selection/a22ac31dda68a114f54133dc184c4a0ec3780356ab5f8915f0f44dfe8856bdbe" :answer/id #uuid "44552cd7-b0d7-581f-831c-897c0eeecf60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{x}-2x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7897/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "51147bac-3264-5105-8f73-eeb85cb5d7e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-7897/selection/66c5631fedcddabdceaad5086f58076ab48c53bc77d675665bfc4d76a9439ce6" :answer-field/choices ["q-7897/selection/355cbdfc9a6b0fbfcec874529de1ee8dfc88ace13e9d7d4cc3bacfcf53c8e7c3" "q-7897/selection/e9af41dd1d69a404c130f636a36b576e034bd76278dbe883bc938617e95e59b7" "q-7897/selection/ffdccedf006adb8d8c243369eaddc427f13a1ea0b11bf6c832a0ffb93d6dcf95" "q-7897/selection/66c5631fedcddabdceaad5086f58076ab48c53bc77d675665bfc4d76a9439ce6" "q-7897/selection/a22ac31dda68a114f54133dc184c4a0ec3780356ab5f8915f0f44dfe8856bdbe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7897" :question/id #uuid "954ee000-a265-58c3-9263-7daaff9ae9c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-7897" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=3x+1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -3 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-3$ or $\\lambda =1$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $1,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha x+\\beta \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha ,\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=0\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n0+2\\alpha -3(\\alpha x+\\beta )=3x+1\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-3\\alpha x+(2\\alpha -3\\beta )=3x+1.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-3\\alpha =3\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ 2\\alpha -3\\beta =1\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-1,\\beta =-1.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-x-1.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-3x}+B{e}^{x}-x-1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-7897/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d86b46c0-e30d-525b-b84e-f8296c78aa8b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7897"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-7902"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+8\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+16y=32x+16.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+8\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+16y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +16 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =4$ is a repeated root, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{-4x}+Bx{e}^{-4x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $1.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $1,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha x+\\beta \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=\\alpha ,\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=0\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation. This gives:\n\n$$\n0+8\\alpha +16(\\alpha x+\\beta )=32x+16\n$$\n\nWe then group the terms on the left-hand side, as follows:\n\n$$\n16\\alpha x+(8\\alpha +16\\beta )=32x+16\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}16\\alpha =32\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ 8\\alpha +16\\beta =16\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =2,\\,\\beta =0.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=2x.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-4x}+Bx{e}^{-4x}+2x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-93830/selection/0adc06d738552a87d1d68b00d5aa18c87d5f8feb95485e248d04614e80bb23b5" :answer/id #uuid "9ce0bb76-fd3b-5d3c-be7e-037c818dd4f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{-3x}+2{x}^{2}-2x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93830/selection/e7a6e41713fd2b028b0262123697e0caf845e5cb4a2283dc2d2412c55741c224" :answer/id #uuid "afaebfdb-2306-5f42-9e4a-4be41e2e138d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{-2x}-{x}^{2}+2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93830/selection/c415b7407d0292f0d5a33d5126506964afbed5fc417f1fc005d22797a881013f" :answer/id #uuid "1bfd82bd-902e-5a2d-a500-4d5ac0709fdf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{-3x}+2{x}^{2}+2x+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93830/selection/a68f9db3e2a15673e39fcb90de763dda5f96d55af4d30a01314bd4a7879bdc62" :answer/id #uuid "41bb8d40-e774-5ff5-b966-37eacfaaf29d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{-3x}-{x}^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93830/selection/d621283b6c26bc1c326006122d15ccffb6ca9688956f6fe451935411160058cc" :answer/id #uuid "5049b73b-a217-57e0-b55e-da248fb5637c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=A{e}^{x}+B{e}^{-2x}+{x}^{2}-2x+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93830/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "59019122-b9a7-598f-a15f-7e1535e654c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93830/selection/0adc06d738552a87d1d68b00d5aa18c87d5f8feb95485e248d04614e80bb23b5" :answer-field/choices ["q-93830/selection/0adc06d738552a87d1d68b00d5aa18c87d5f8feb95485e248d04614e80bb23b5" "q-93830/selection/e7a6e41713fd2b028b0262123697e0caf845e5cb4a2283dc2d2412c55741c224" "q-93830/selection/c415b7407d0292f0d5a33d5126506964afbed5fc417f1fc005d22797a881013f" "q-93830/selection/a68f9db3e2a15673e39fcb90de763dda5f96d55af4d30a01314bd4a7879bdc62" "q-93830/selection/d621283b6c26bc1c326006122d15ccffb6ca9688956f6fe451935411160058cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93830" :question/id #uuid "ffa40815-fb21-52fd-a6a4-4ce989aef44c" :question/math-academy-id "q-93830" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+7\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+12y=24{x}^{2}+4x+2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+7\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+12y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+7\\lambda +12 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)(\\lambda +3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =-4$ or $\\lambda =-3$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}$ is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{-3x}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular integral ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $2.$ Therefore, we assume that the particular integral is also a polynomial of degree $2,$ i.e.\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma \n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta $, and $\\gamma $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=2\\alpha x+\\beta ,\\,\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}=2\\alpha .\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ $\\beta ,$ and $\\gamma ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation. This gives:\n\n$$\n2\\alpha +7(2\\alpha x+\\beta )+12(\\alpha {x}^{2}+\\beta x+\\gamma )=24{x}^{2}+4x+2\n$$\n\nWe then group the terms on the left-hand side, as follows:\n\n$$\n12\\alpha {x}^{2}+(14\\alpha +12\\beta )x+(2\\alpha +7\\beta +12\\gamma )=24{x}^{2}+4x+2\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}12\\alpha =24\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,{x}^{2}) \\\\ 14\\alpha +12\\beta =4\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,x) \\\\ 2\\alpha +7\\beta +12\\gamma =2\\, & (\\text{equating the constants})\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =2,\\beta =-2,\\gamma =1.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=2{x}^{2}-2x+1.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by \n\n$$\ny={y}_{c}+{y}_{p}\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-4x}+B{e}^{-3x}+2{x}^{2}-2x+1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-93830/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "41bccbd5-3d0c-5f00-b506-97b8f83c5472"] :knowledge-poi